From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:27:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 089/105] N1 stage A: W4A16 NVFP4 GEMV kernel, quantiser,
 numerics check and FP8 head-to-head bench

Adds w4a16_nvfp4_gemv: a Triton skinny GEMV (M <= 16) over the same NVFP4 format the
experts use -- [N, K/2] uint8 codes, [N, K/16] E4M3 block scales, one global scale.
Structure mirrors w8a16_gemv (split-K reduced in-launch, split-store epilogue, PDL,
shared scratch); the new part is the A-load: nibble unpack via tl.join plus the in-house engine's
fp16 bit-trick dequant, whose product with the E4M3 block scale is exact in bf16.

The quantiser deliberately matches the project's reference NVFP4 emulation
bit-for-bit. Getting there needed two fixes: the
global scale must be *multiplied* in the fork's own form (a 1 ulp difference flips ~1 %
of E4M3 block scales, which sit exactly on tie points), and E2M1 rounding must break
ties to even.

Recorded in specs/N1_LOG.md: the brief's roofline premise is wrong for the two lm_head
shapes (they run at 96-98 % of the read roof, not 78-85 %), which moves the 4-bit
break-even from 40 % to 55 % of roof and caps the realistic prize near 1 % of the step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
